    {
      "platform": "windows",
      "version": "2026.07-1",
      "release_date": "2026-07-29",
      "release_notes": "Python version: 3.14.6\n\nUser-facing Changes\n- Conda has been updated to v26.5.3. See the conda blog post for highlights about the conda 26.5.x releases.\n- Anaconda3 now ships with Python 3.14 (upgraded from Python 3.13).\n- This release includes the anaconda-channel-guide plugin, which notifies users when packages not found in their configured channels are available through other Anaconda channels, including the new main-x channel.\n- Added jedi and libxml2 to the package list.\n- Removed pycurl and scrapy from the package list.\n- Added architecture checks for macOS PKG and SH installers. Attempting to install a macOS installer onto an Intel Mac will now lead to an error at the beginning of the installation.\n- Updated the macOS PKG installer error message when the target directory already exists. The error message now includes a link to the uninstall instructions.\n- The option to choose a specific install location has been removed from the macOS PKG installers for this release due to a bug specifically with macOS Tahoe (version 26).\n- Each installation now contains an .installer.info file with information about the installer to simplify diagnostics.\n\nBug fixes\n- The ~/.anaconda directory is now deleted when choosing to remove user data during uninstallation.\n- Fixed an issue where macOS PKG installers would fail when file ownership in $HOME could not be changed.\n- Fixed a bug in EXE installers that prevented uninstallation if the installation was added to PATH.\n- Fixed a bug for EXE installers that caused package extraction to fail with Windows Defender Application Control.",
      "release_notes_url": "https://www.anaconda.com/docs/getting-started/anaconda/release-notes#anaconda-2026-07-1",
      "manifest_version": "1.12.0",
      "manifest_dir": "manifests/a/Anaconda/Anaconda3/2026.07-1",
